# Benchmark results

The results of the benchmarks in `bench/`: every PEGO backend (closure, recursive and iterative bytecode VMs, Go
parsers generated by `pego gen`) and, where a comparable parser exists, the Go standard library. What the benchmarks
measure, the analysis of these results, and the history of the optimizations behind them are in
[performance.md](performance.md).

This file is generated: `go run ./bench/report` runs the benchmarks, saves the raw results to
[`bench/results.txt`](../bench/results.txt) and writes this file from them; `go run ./bench/report -in
bench/results.txt` rewrites it from saved results. Do not edit it by hand: a test checks that it matches the results.

## Run

Measured on {{meta "date"}} at commit {{meta "commit"}} with {{meta "go"}} on {{meta "cpu"}} ({{meta "goos"}}/{{meta "goarch"}}, {{meta "cores"}} cores){{if hasMeta "load"}}, with a load average of {{meta "load"}} (1, 5 and 15 minutes) when the run started{{end}}.
Times and memory are per operation, the median of {{runs "Parse/JSON/closure/codepoints"}} runs. Factors in parentheses are relative to the closure backend (lower is faster), except where a table says otherwise.

